2|0@martialarts^1438715186#ctrex1o:osotogary_$:I think you're viewing it out of context. Correia said that she hoped that Rousey wouldn't kill herself after she lost, knowing that Rousey lost her father to suicide at a very young age. I've never lost anyone to suicide, so I cannot imagine how deeply one can be wounded by it. Sure, Rousey said something that, out of context, is pretty childish. But I think you shouldn't let it taint her as a "brawler" or a "not worthy of the title Judoka" because she got worked up at a woman who insulted her father's memory. Sure, she is a role model, and does many things a role model would do, like donating her belt to a judo school in Brazil after her victory. But she is also a person, and I think that you are holding her to an unreasonable standard because of the context through which you view her, as someone who turned her back on the IJF and Judo and became one of the most successful MMA fighters of all time. The reality is that she is a good role model, and is actually pretty great with kids (to the point that Gallowboob is posting gifs of her interacting with children for karma), she just competes in a sport that you feel morally opposed to.
