3|0@martialarts^1438723392#ctrkod4:osotogary_$:I think you've got a lot of biases that you need to figure out that aren't really related to MMA at all. Sounds like you've got beef with western civilization in general. How is a combat sport imperialistic? Do you have beef with the concept of spectators? It's just a different art with different rules, dude. Do you hate all striking arts, because of the risk of head trauma? Ground and pound isn't really that different from punching someone on your feet. And refs in the UFC typically end fights as soon after the knockout as they can, there's no eight or ten count for someone to get back up after they get knocked out, like in western boxing and some types of kung fu. Also are you saying there is any more morality in IJF judo? when I was doing judo, I was at a very grassroots place, in the basement of a church. It was comparatively very cheap, and everyone was very kind. There were kids classes that everyone helped out with if they had the time. Everyone was genuinely interested in each other's well being. This is what I think judo is all about, and I'm experiencing a similarly warm environment as I make the transition to a less traditional grappling art. But the IJF is a different story. They do not represent all of judo. All I've heard about them paints them as a huge, fairly corrupt and definitely bloated bureaucracy that, as you said yourself, limits valuable techniques for the average practitioner. Why does turning your back on that make you a bad person? Why does wanting recognition for your efforts make you a bad person? Why does punching people in the octagon make you a bad person? Rousey is still a judoka. She is still an Olympic medalist. She still does her uchikomis and practices hard. She also hits a bag, spars with no gi, and does all of the things that make MMA different from judo. But she is still a judoka, and that's part of the reason that she is so successful in MMA. Edit: grammar. Also, sorry about the wall of text. I don't comment often and I don't know how to make paragraph breaks on reddit yet.
